H9 rcbot_mm.dll -- built from patched source

Change 5 (see rcbot-patch/README.txt): the TS weapon-learning crash fix
(CBotGAValues::get on an empty vector -- root cause and symptom both in the
README). Building it against the pinned upstream (APGRoboCop/rcbotold @
v1.51b13, 43ecb57) surfaced that the project's existing follow-command patch
(README CHANGE 3) had never actually compiled from a clean checkout + the
tracked rcbot-ts-teams.patch alone -- its .cpp logic was all there, but two
method prototypes it needs were never added to bot.h, and two small helper
functions it calls (CBotGlobals::GetBot, CBotSquads::createSquad) had no body
anywhere in this repo. Fixed along the way, all in bot.h now part of this
project's tracked src/:
  - SetFollowTarget/ConsoleCommandFollow: prototypes added to the CBot class
    (bodies were already correct, just never declared).
  - CBotGlobals::GetBot: implemented for real -- m_Bots[ENTINDEX(edict)-1],
    the same indexing convention already used throughout this file.
  - CBotSquads::createSquad: stubbed to return nullptr. Real squad
    construction isn't implemented; SetFollowTarget already null-checks the
    result, so the follow command proceeds without squad-specific behavior
    (formation/combat-type) instead of failing to build. Not a regression --
    there was no working createSquad to regress from.
  - CBotTasks::RemoveTask doesn't exist (only a commented-out stub does);
    the follow command's cleanup path now calls the real equivalent,
    RemoveSimilarTask.
Also: SeedTSWeaponSelectValues (what Change 5's own patch called to refill a
short individual) doesn't exist either -- inlined the same per-value seeding
the adjacent DISABLE_WEAPON_LEARN branch already does, via add() (confirmed
growing) rather than set() (bounds behavior on a short vector unconfirmed).
And CBotGAValues::size() isn't a member -- every size check uses the
existing returnVector()->size() instead.

Below is the diff against the previously-tracked bot.cpp (the sum of Change 5
plus the fixes above); ga.cpp's one-line size-check fix and bot.h's new
declarations are summarized above rather than diffed, since bot.h was not
previously part of this project's tracked src/ at all.

--- /d/Downloads/TSM/backups/rcbot-tsweaps-crash-20261022-075500/bot.cpp.before	2026-10-22 14:26:41.603931800 -0400
+++ /d/Downloads/TSM/rcbot-patch/src/bot.cpp	2026-10-22 14:39:19.737715500 -0400
@@ -3002,6 +3002,20 @@
 				m_pTSWeaponSelect = static_cast<CBotGAValues*>(costs);
 				m_pTSWeaponSelect->setFitness(0);
 
+				// an individual with fewer values than a bot's weapon choice has (from learned data that did not load)
+				if (m_pTSWeaponSelect->returnVector()->size() < 8)
+				{
+					// SeedTSWeaponSelectValues doesn't exist in this codebase; inline the
+					// same seeding the DISABLE_WEAPON_LEARN branch right below already does
+					// per-value, via add() (confirmed growing, ga.h: emplace_back) rather
